  "notes": "Built from homeassistant/components/met/weather.py and the PyMetno 0.13.0 library it calls; core has no met snapshot and its test mock carries no forecast. Values are realistic for Oslo (Europe/Oslo) in early November. Current: no apparent_temperature, visibility or ozone are ever set. Each attribute appears only when met.no's timeseries[0] carries it: wind_gust_speed (wind_speed_of_gust) only inside the Nordic short-range model area; cloud_coverage and uv_index are floats with one decimal (uv_index is ultraviolet_index_clear_sky). Condition 'sunny' becomes 'clear-night' when the sun is down. Hourly: up to 48 entries starting at the next whole hour (now + 1 h), datetimes in UTC; precipitation_probability only where met.no gives probability_of_precipitation (next_1_hours, Nordic area); wind_gust_speed only where gusts exist. Daily: 6 entries, today plus 5 days, each stamped 12:00 local time expressed in UTC (so today's entry can lie before now); temperature/templow are the max/min of that local day's remaining time steps (today only counts hours from the first time step on); precipitation is the day's summed amount; humidity comes from the first time step at or after noon; daily never carries cloud_coverage, pressure or dew_point. Any forecast key is dropped when its value is None. precipitation_probability is a float (e.g. 34.6), wind_bearing a float. Options: track_home only changes the device name; a legacy separate hourly entity is removed at setup, so there is one entity with daily and hourly. Change for realism: current dew point 4.7 -> 5.4, to agree with 7.6 C and 86 %.",
